# SICL Web — SQLite migration status

## Scope

This document records the isolated SQLite repository work in SICL Web.

The SQLite adapter and repositories are experimental and isolated.
They do not replace the production MySQL database module.
No MySQL migration or production backend switch is authorized by this work.

## User repository upsert behavior

The SQLite user repository must preserve the intended MySQL upsert behavior:

- `openId` is required.
- Fields omitted from a partial upsert are not overwritten.
- `createdAt` remains unchanged on conflict.
- `updatedAt` is refreshed on upsert.
- Owner role defaults to `admin` when no role is supplied.
- An explicit role is respected.
- An upsert without other update fields refreshes `lastSignedIn`.
- An omitted `lastSignedIn` does not overwrite an existing timestamp.
- A falsy `lastSignedIn` value, including zero, receives a current timestamp on INSERT.
- An explicit zero remains zero in the conflict UPDATE set, matching the MySQL implementation.

## Regression history

MO23-S3-AN exposed a failing assertion for the zero timestamp INSERT fallback.

The cause was the repository assigning zero to both:
- the INSERT values,
- the conflict UPDATE set.

The correction now separates those semantics:
- INSERT values use the current timestamp when the supplied value is falsy.
- Conflict UPDATE retains the explicitly supplied value, including zero.

